# Safety-First Philosophy - C# and .NET

## Core Principle
**NEVER CRASH**. In a bullet-hell game, a crash means the player loses their progress. Always provide safe defaults, validate inputs, and handle errors gracefully.

## Null Safety and Node Validation

### IsInstanceValid() - The Golden Rule
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Always validate before using nodes
public void AttackTarget()
{
    if (_targetNode == null || !IsInstanceValid(_targetNode))
    {
        GD.PushError("[Enemy] Target node is invalid, aborting attack");
        return;
    }
    
    var bullet = EntityFactory.SpawnBullet("enemy_basic", GlobalPosition, CalculateDirection());
    if (bullet != null)
    {
        bullet.Target = _targetNode;
    }
}

// ❌ BAD: Assume node exists
public void AttackTarget()
{
    var bullet = EntityFactory.SpawnBullet("enemy_basic", GlobalPosition, CalculateDirection());
    bullet.Target = _targetNode; // CRASH if _targetNode was freed!
}
```

