## Type Validation

### Runtime Type Checks
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Explicit type validation
public void ApplyDamageToEntity(object entity, int damage)
{
    if (entity == null || !IsInstanceValid(entity as Node))
    {
        GD.PushError("[Combat] Entity is invalid");
        return;
    }
    
    if (entity is not Node node)
    {
        GD.PushError($"[Combat] Entity is not a Node: {entity.GetType()}");
        return;
    }
    
    if (!node.HasMethod("take_damage"))
    {
        GD.PushError($"[Combat] Entity {node.Name} does not implement take_damage()");
        return;
    }
    
    node.Call("take_damage", damage);
}

// ✅ GOOD: Safe casting with validation
public Enemy GetEnemyFromCollision(Node2D body)
{
    if (body == null || !IsInstanceValid(body))
        return null;
    
    if (body is not Enemy enemy)
    {
        GD.PushWarning($"[Collision] Body {body.Name} is not an Enemy");
        return null;
    }
    
    return enemy;
}
```

## Pooling Safety

### Complete State Reset
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Thorough pooling reset
public void ResetForPool()
{
    // 1. Disconnect signals (prevents memory leaks)
    DisconnectAllSignals();
    
    // 2. Reset transform
    GlobalPosition = Vector2.Zero;
    Rotation = 0.0f;
    Scale = Vector2.One;
    
    // 3. Reset physics
    Velocity = Vector2.Zero;
    if (this is RigidBody2D rigidBody)
    {
        rigidBody.LinearVelocity = Vector2.Zero;
        rigidBody.AngularVelocity = 0.0f;
    }
    
    // 4. Reset gameplay state
    Health = MaxHealth;
    IsAlive = true;
    StateMachineState = State.Idle;
    
    // 5. Clear references (prevent leaks)
    TargetNode = null;
    OwnerEntity = null;
    _cachedPlayer = null;
    
    // 6. Reset visual
    Modulate = Colors.White;
    Visible = false;
    
    // 7. Disable processing
    ProcessMode = ProcessModeEnum.Disabled;
    SetPhysicsProcess(false);
    SetProcess(false);
    
    // 8. Clear timers
    _attackCooldown = 0.0f;
    _invulnerabilityTimer = 0.0f;
}

// ❌ BAD: Incomplete reset (stale state lingers)
public void ResetForPool()
{
    Position = Vector2.Zero;
    Visible = false;
    // Forgot: signals, velocity, health, references, processing!
}
```

## Defensive Programming Checklist

For every function that:
- [ ] Accesses a node → Validate with `IsInstanceValid()`
- [ ] Accesses an array → Check bounds with `index < Count`
- [ ] Accesses a dictionary → Use `TryGetValue(key, out value)`
- [ ] Performs division → Check denominator != 0
- [ ] Awaits a signal → Re-validate nodes after await
- [ ] Modifies scene tree → Use `CallDeferred()` if in lifecycle method
- [ ] Connects a signal → Check `IsConnected()` first
- [ ] Accepts external data → Validate and provide safe defaults
- [ ] Returns null → Document why and handle at call site
- [ ] Fails critically → Use `GD.PushError()` with detailed message
- [ ] Has recoverable issue → Use `GD.PushWarning()` with context

## Error Recovery Examples

### Graceful Stage Loading Failure
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Multi-layer fallback
public void LoadStage(int stageNumber)
{
    var stageDef = StageTemplateManager.GetStage(stageNumber);
    
    if (stageDef == null)
    {
        GD.PushWarning($"[StageController] Stage {stageNumber} not found, looping to stage 1");
        stageDef = StageTemplateManager.GetStage(1);
    }
    
    if (stageDef == null)
    {
        GD.PushError("[StageController] Critical: Stage 1 missing! Generating emergency stage");
        stageDef = CreateEmergencyStage();
    }
    
    StartStage(stageDef);
}

private StageDefinition CreateEmergencyStage()
{
    var emergencyStage = new StageDefinition
    {
        StageNumber = 1,
        StageName = "Emergency Stage",
        Waves = new List<WaveDefinition> { CreateSimpleWave() }
    };
    return emergencyStage;
}
```

### Robust Entity Spawning
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Handle spawn failures gracefully
public List<Enemy> SpawnEnemyFormation(string templateId, int count)
{
    var spawnedEnemies = new List<Enemy>();
    int failedSpawns = 0;
    
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        var enemy = EntityFactory.SpawnEnemy(templateId, CalculatePosition(i), Vector2.Down);
        
        if (enemy == null)
        {
            failedSpawns++;
            if (failedSpawns > count / 2)
            {
                GD.PushError("[Spawner] Failed to spawn >50% of enemies, aborting formation");
                break;
            }
            continue;
        }
        
        spawnedEnemies.Add(enemy);
    }
    
    if (failedSpawns > 0)
    {
        GD.PushWarning($"[Spawner] {failedSpawns}/{count} enemy spawns failed");
    }
    
    return spawnedEnemies;
}
```

## Summary

Safety is NON-NEGOTIABLE. Every node access, array index, dictionary key, and division must be validated. Use defensive programming everywhere, provide safe defaults for all failures, and NEVER crash the player's game.